.TH VALLOC 3 "May 12, 1986"
.UC 3
.SH NAME
valloc \- aligned memory allocator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
char *
valloc(\fIunsigned int size\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.ft B
valloc is obsoleted by the current version of malloc.
.ft R
.PP
.B valloc
on 2.11BSD simply calls
.BR malloc (3)
with
.I size
as the argument.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B valloc
returns a null pointer (0) if there is no available memory
or if the arena has been detectably corrupted by storing outside the bounds
of a block.
.SH NOTES
Memory allocated by
.B valloc
should be released by calling
.B free
